From 3b714699d9fecd1384cc4aa863dfd281496bfa50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:20:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250: fix full resolution camera
 capture

Set the camera NoC AXI clock rate on SM8250. It stayed at 19.2 MHz,
so RDI capture of the full resolution sensor modes never completed.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ...-vfe-Set-the-camnoc_axi_src-clock-ra.patch | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/APKBUILD   |  4 +-
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0013-media-qcom-camss-vfe-Set-the-camnoc_axi_src-clock-ra.patch

diff --git a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0013-media-qcom-camss-vfe-Set-the-camnoc_axi_src-clock-ra.patch b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0013-media-qcom-camss-vfe-Set-the-camnoc_axi_src-clock-ra.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1f54fc0b31
--- /dev/null
+++ b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8250/0013-media-qcom-camss-vfe-Set-the-camnoc_axi_src-clock-ra.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+From 5634b94b50ccc706e6c8eff1db0e529f4736e2da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:15:47 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Set the camnoc_axi_src clock rate
+
+On SM8250 the rate table for the camera NoC AXI clock is attached to
+"camnoc_axi_src", while vfe_set_clock_rates() only scales clocks named
+"camnoc_axi" or "camnoc_rt_axi". The clock is therefore never set and
+stays at 19.2 MHz while streaming.
+
+At that rate the bus cannot drain long lines: RDI capture of full
+resolution modes (4208x3120 and 4656x3496 RAW10, about 5.3 KiB per
+line) never completes a frame, and the bus reports a CCIF violation
+for the write master, while binned modes with shorter lines still
+work. Scale "camnoc_axi_src" with the pixel clock like the other
+camnoc clocks.
+
+Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 1 +
+ 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
+
+diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+index 319d19158..8d3cffc28 100644
+--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
++++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+@@ -919,6 +919,7 @@ static int vfe_match_clock_names(struct vfe_device *vfe,
+ 		!strcmp(clock->name, vfe_lite_name) ||
+ 		!strcmp(clock->name, "vfe_lite") ||
+ 		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_axi") ||
++		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_axi_src") ||
+ 		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_rt_axi"));
+ }
+ 
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
